   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Saying hello and goodbye",
     "texto": [
      "**Merhaba** can be used at any time of day. **Günaydın** means good morning; **iyi akşamlar** means good afternoon or good evening when you arrive.",
      "To say goodbye, the person leaving says **hoşça kal** to the person staying, and the person staying replies **güle güle** to the person leaving.",
      "**Lütfen** means «please» and **teşekkürler** means «thank you»."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Asking how someone is",
     "texto": [
      "**Nasılsın?** is informal, for one person. You answer **İyiyim** (I'm fine) or **İyiyim, teşekkürler** (I'm fine, thanks).",
      "**Nasılsınız?** is the polite or plural form. The ending **-sınız** marks the formal or plural form."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    }
   ]
  },
